parts.text:
All confirmed:
- Docs Clínicos sub-itens: `/app/documentos-clinicos/diario`, `/app/documentos-clinicos/frequencia`, `/app/documentos-clinicos/plano`
- Laudos: `/app/laudos` (registered in app.routes.ts, no menu item)

Now I'll restructure. Plan:

1. Extend the nav item type: `{ id, label, icon, route?, children?, count? }`. TypeScript inferred array — I'll add a type.
2. New structure:
   - Keep all items, but:
     - Remove individual items `documentos`, `documentos-clinicos`, `biblioteca`, `laudos`, `solicitacoes`, `lgpd`
     - Add a group item `documentos` with icon `folder_open`, label 'Documentos', `children`:
       - Documentos (arquivos) → `/app/documentos` (icon folder)
       - Docs Clínicos → `/app/documentos-clinicos` (icon note) with children? The user chose "Direto no submenu" — so Diário, Frequência, Plano de Intervenção as direct sub-items. So children of "Documentos" group:
         - `{ label: 'Arquivos', icon: 'folder', route: '/app/documentos' }`
         - `{ label: 'Diário de Sessões', icon: 'edit_note', route: '/app/documentos-clinicos/diario' }`
         - `{ label: 'Frequência', icon: 'fact_check'... }` — wait fact_check is used by Protocolos. Use 'checklist' or 'event_note'. Let me pick icons:
           - Diário de Sessões: `edit_note`
           - Frequência: `format_list_bulleted` or `checklist` → `checklist` fits
           - Plano de Intervenção: `assignment` or `planner` → `assignment` 
         - Biblioteca: `menu_book` → `/app/biblioteca`
         - Laudos: `description` → `/app/laudos`
         - Solicitações: `assignment_turned_in` → `/app/solicitacoes`
         - LGPD: `gpp_good` → `/app/lgpd`
   - Question: should Docs Clínicos hub page remain reachable? The user said "Cada um vira um sub-item clicável; a página hub de cards deixa de ser necessária no menu". So no "Docs Clínicos" hub item — direct sub-items. Good.
   - The group click: expand/collapse. But should clicking "Documentos" also navigate? Better: clicking toggles expansion (with chevron). Keep `/app/documentos` reachable via sub-item "Arquivos".

3. Expansion state: `expandedMenus = signal<Set<string>>(new Set())` or a simple boolean signal `documentosOpen`. Since only one group for now, but make it generic: `expanded = signal(new Set<string>())`, `toggleGroup(id)`.

4. When sidebar collapsed (w-20), the submenu should hide — simplest: only render children when `sidebarOpen()` is true. Also auto-expand when... keep simple: hide children when collapsed.

5. Auto-expand group if current route is inside it (on init / route change) — nice UX. When user navigates to `/app/documentos-clinicos/diario` directly, the group should be expanded. I'll implement: in updatePageTitle (already subscribes to router events), check if current URL starts with any group's child route → expand that group. Also highlight active child.

6. routerLinkActive for children: the child link is active when URL matches. `/app/documentos` child vs group `/app/documentos` — careful: routerLinkActive on `/app/documentos` also matches `/app/documentos-clinicos`? RouterLinkActive matches prefix by default for... no — default is "prefix" match: `/app/documentos` matches `/app/documentos-clinicos` too. Use `[routerLinkActiveOptions]="{ exact: true }"` for the Arquivos item.

7. Update `titles` map: add `laudos`. Keep existing keys. Also docs-clinicos hub title fine.

8. Badge counts: group doesn't need count. Keep count only on agenda.

